        "timestamp": 1778786445,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'A desire to lower the temperature on both sides', expert says as Trump meets Xi Americas Issued on: 14/05/2026 - 21:20 Modified: 14/05/2026 - 21:22 Presidents Xi Jinping and Donald Trump started a crucial series of meetings in Beijing on Thursday in the U.S.-China summit. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Garret Martin, Lecturer and Co-Director Transatlantic Policy Center at the American University School of International Service, says that \"what we saw today was not much in substance but at the very least a desire to lower the temperature on both sides\". Hantavirus: US cruiseship passenger gives quarantine room tour 13/05/2026 Americas Denver airport: Surveillance footage shows moment aircraft fatally struck runway intruder 12/05/2026 Americas Pentagon releases new files on UFOs 09/05/2026 Americas Flamboyant US entrepreneur and CNN founder Ted Turner dead at 87 06/05/2026 Americas United States: Los Angeles fire suspect had grudge against wealthy 06/05/2026 Americas Donald Trump renews pressure and plans to hike tariffs on EU cars 06/05/2026 Americas Three killed after small plane crashes in southeastern Brazil 05/05/2026 Americas Stars shine at eccentric Met Gala, fashion's biggest night 05/05/2026 Americas Anti-Bezos campaign urges Met Gala boycott in New York 04/05/2026 Americas"
